 "notes": [
  "Maintainer rebuild for the release example on the rebuilt Stage 2 scene (three-slot holder): every subgoal re-executed with the current executor and realistic contact friction. stage3_r4's plan structure was the starting point (tilted insert, let-go, rim push with a left brace); its cell pinch (34 mm up) no longer seats with the realistic friction and was replaced.",
  "Subgoal 3 (insert): the cell is carried tilted 60 deg (its - end low) into slot 2, the near slot (spring at the holder's lower-left end), with the top edge of its - face pressing the spring's contact plate 1.5 mm, then let go: it drops into the slot with its - end on the slot floor and its + end resting on the far end wall (not yet seated, as the Stage 1 goal allows). A deeper hold is impossible for this hand: at 45 deg and less the curled fingers straddling the cell reach the slot divider, the side wall and the table.",
  "Subgoal 4 (both): the left hand braces the holder's spring-end wall with two fingertips while the right hand presses the + end rim down and toward the spring (wrist force capped at 20 N): the spring compresses and the cell drops in and lies flat between the contacts (spring 2.4 mm compressed).",
  "Subgoal 5 (both): the right hand lifts off the seated cell while the left still holds the holder, then the left lets go; both arms return home and the holder rests with the cell seated.",
  "The free holder slides and turns on the cloth when the cell drops in at the let-go and under the press (10 mm / 8 deg over the episode); the human's holder also shifts during the press.",
  "Stage 2 was rebuilt during this pass (three-slot holder; its rigid decorative leads dropped after they sank 12 mm into the tabletop when the holder tilted at the let-go: object_visual_penetration_audit); the episode was re-executed on the rebuilt scene.",
  "Both arm stations are moved -0.075 m (place_arm_stations); every tool, audit and the Stage 4 package use scene_stations.xml."
 ],
